# Seamless Login via URL Payload

The goal is to provide a way to log a user in directly via a URL containing `UserName`, `Token`, and `timestamp`. We will create a **new Action method (`DirectLogin`)** to catch this payload, keeping the existing [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) GET method unmodified. To avoid duplicating code, we will extract the existing session generation code into a **new helper method (`CreateUserSession`)** so both the `DirectLogin` method and the [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) POST method (for normal login) share the session setup logic.

